  "Win and method chances come from the same model as the bets: the blended moneyline (market plus model) sets who wins, the model's outcome table splits each win into KO, submission or decision and the finish into rounds.",
  "Volume points (strikes, takedowns, control, knockdowns) are each fighter's per-minute rates from earlier UFC fights, mixed half and half with what his opponent usually allows, times the minutes each outcome implies. Winners out-land their projected rate and losers fall short; both effects are fitted on every UFC fight since 2010.",
  "Projection = sum over outcomes of chance x (win bonus + volume). The 10th to 90th percentile range comes from simulating 4,000 fights. Checked walk-forward on 2018-2026: projections were calibrated (58.0 projected vs 58.8 scored per fighter) with correlation 0.45 to actual points.",
